EXTERNAL DEPENDENCIES AND BUNDLED CONTENT

oneko sprites — the `neko`, `tora`, and `dog` artwork in assets/ and
vendor/oneko/ is NOT covered by the MIT licence above. It is public-domain artwork from
oneko 1.2.sakura.5 by Masayuki Koba, modified by Tatsuya Kato, redistributed
under the Public Domain declaration of that package. The oneko sets whose
rights are reserved (bsd, sakura, tomoyo) are NOT included here. Full source,
checksum, and reasoning: vendor/oneko/PROVENANCE.md.

Turtle sprites — the original `turtle` and `turtle-shell` artwork in assets/
and its source in tools/turtle_sprites.py are covered by the MIT licence above.

Runtime — this plugin requires only Omarchy 4 and python3, both already
present on an Omarchy system. It bundles and runs one helper of its own,
bin/navbar-cat-cursor, which reads the pointer position from the Hyprland IPC
socket. It installs nothing, downloads nothing, requires no elevated
privileges, and makes no network connections.

Build tooling — tools/build-sprites.py requires Pillow, and is only needed to
regenerate the spritesheets. The generated sheets are committed, so no build
step is involved in installing or running the plugin.
